items/thm-no-continuous-logarithm-on-the-punctured-complex-plane.md:48:1.1 Suppose such a continuous $L$ exists and put $h(t)=L(\gamma(t))-it$. By [L2], [L3], and [L5], $\gamma$, $L\circ\gamma$, and $h$ are continuous on $[0,2\pi]$. [assume-contra, L2, L3, L5]
